{"id": "26244", "revid": "2196717", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=26244", "title": "Othello", "text": "Othello is a city of about 8,500 people in the Columbia River Plateau of Washington State. It's a food processing hub for the region, processing approximately 1.5 billion pounds (680 kt) of frozen potato products annually, comprising 15 percent of production in North America.\nGet in.\nOthello is at the intersection of State Route 17 (WA-17) and State Route 26 (WA-26)."}
{"id": "26245", "revid": "2217354", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=26245", "title": "Other destinations", "text": "This page includes destinations that do not fit any other category, as well as listings of sites around the world.\nThis page is a catch-all for travel destinations and concepts that don't neatly belong to any single continent or country in Wikivoyage's geographical hierarchy. It includes broad thematic regions (such as the Tropics or Mediterranean Sea), collections of remote or isolated places (like ocean islands not tied to a mainland), and global lists of special sites (e.g., UNESCO designations). For most travelers, start with the continent or country pages instead; use this page when searching for unusual, boundary-crossing, or \"everywhere\" ideas."}
